iv></figure><p id=\"49f4\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">In this tutorial, I\u2019ll walk you through how to create quick professional cloud architecture diagrams using Python\u2019s <a class=\"af hb\" href=\"https://diagrams.mingrammer.com/\" rel=\"noopener ugc nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Diagrams</a> library and the Cursor editor. We\u2019ll build a comprehensive AWS multi-account architecture diagram for a fictional startup called Innovate Inc., following their requirements and iteratively improving the visualization.</p><h1 id=\"1b4e\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Why use code for Architecture Diagrams?</h1><p id=\"1a54\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Before diving in, let\u2019s consider why you might want to use code instead of traditional diagramming tools:</p><ul class=\"\"><li id=\"02b1\" class=\"op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Version control</strong>: Your diagrams live in your repository alongside your code</li><li id=\"d301\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Reproducibility</strong>: Anyone can generate the same diagram</li><li id=\"3517\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Maintainability</strong>: Easy to update as your infrastructure evolves</li><li id=\"1c50\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Consistency</strong>: Standardized visual elements and styling</li></ul><h1 id=\"81c0\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Prerequisites</h1><ul class=\"\"><li id=\"3087\" class=\"op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\"><a class=\"af hb\" href=\"https://cursor.sh/\" rel=\"noopener ugc nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Cursor</a> \u2014 An AI-powered code editor</li><li id=\"f84f\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\">Python 3.7+ installed</li><li id=\"b465\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\">Basic understanding of AWS services</li><li id=\"7462\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj ql qm qn bk\">The Diagrams library (<code class=\"cx qt qu qv qw b\">pip install diagrams</code>)</li></ul><h1 id=\"077b\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Project setup</h1><p id=\"2042\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Let\u2019s start by setting up our project in Cursor:</p><ol class=\"\"><li id=\"749d\" class=\"op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Create a new directory for your project: <code class=\"cx qt qu qv qw b\">mkdir innovate_inc &amp;&amp; cd innovate_inc</code></li><li id=\"bf7e\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Open this directory in Cursor</li><li id=\"9e5b\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Create a new Python file: <code class=\"cx qt qu qv qw b\">innovate_arch.py</code></li></ol><h1 id=\"9abc\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Step 1: Understanding the requirements</h1><p id=\"4463\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Before writing any code, we need to understand what we\u2019re trying to visualize.</p><p id=\"d825\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">You might have already created an infrastructure design document, which you can use in ChatGPT or another AI tool to help you create the initial requirements document for the diagram. You can modify this outline later as you wish.</p><p id=\"a2ae\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">Example RD:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"2d7b\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Infrastructure Diagram using Diagrams Library (Python) for Innovate Inc.<br/><br/>## Overview<br/>This document specifies the requirements for creating a cloud infrastructure diagram using the [Diagrams](https://diagrams.mingrammer.com/) Python library. The diagram will cover the multi-account AWS setup, networking, compute, database services, CI/CD integration, and the static frontend hosting solution using CloudFront and S3.<br/><br/>## Objective<br/>- **Visualize AWS Multi-Account Structure:**  <br/>  Illustrate separate AWS accounts for Management, Development, Staging, and Production, along with their associated VPCs and resources.<br/>- **Depict Compute, Database, and Networking Components:**  <br/>  Show Amazon EKS clusters, RDS for PostgreSQL, public/private subnet configuration, NAT Gateways, and Client VPN for secure remote access.<br/>- **Include Static Frontend Hosting:**  <br/>  Incorporate CloudFront and S3 for hosting the React single-page application (SPA) to enable fast, secure, and cost-effective delivery of static assets.<br/>- **Integrate CI/CD and GitOps Elements:**  <br/>  Represent automated build/deploy processes through GitHub Actions (or similar) and GitOps practices.<br/><br/>## Stakeholders<br/>- **Cloud/DevOps Engineers:** Responsible for building and managing the infrastructure.<br/>- **Security Team:** Ensures that security best practices are incorporated.<br/>- **Developers:** Use the diagram for understanding deployment workflows and environment isolation.<br/>- **Management:** Reviews governance, cost management, and operational efficiency.<br/><br/>## Functional Requirements<br/>1. **AWS Account Segmentation:**<br/>   - **Management Account:** For centralized governance (IAM Identity Center, logging).<br/>   - **Development Account:** For experimental and developmental workloads.<br/>   - **Staging Account:** For pre-production testing mirroring production configurations.<br/>   - **Production Account:** For live applications with strict security and performance requirements.<br/>2. **VPC and Network Components:**<br/>   - Each account contains its own VPC with public subnets (hosting ALBs, NAT Gateways) and private subnets (hosting EKS clusters and RDS instances).<br/>   - Utilize NAT Gateways for outbound Internet access from private subnets.<br/>   - Include AWS Client VPN for secure remote access.<br/>3. **Compute and Database:**<br/>   - **Amazon EKS:** Used for container orchestration, deployed in separate clusters per account.<br/>   - **RDS for PostgreSQL:** Deployed in private subnets with Multi-AZ configurations in production.<br/>4. **Static Frontend Hosting:**<br/>   - **Amazon S3:** Hosts the static assets of the React frontend.<br/>   - **Amazon \r\n5dd3\r\nCloudFront:** Acts as a CDN for global content delivery, caching, and enhanced security (with HTTPS termination).<br/>5. **CI/CD and GitOps:**<br/>   - Automated pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions) to build, test, and deploy container images.<br/>   - GitOps tools (e.g., Argo CD) to manage deployments on EKS.<br/><br/>## Non-Functional Requirements<br/>- **Scalability:**  <br/>  The diagram should be easily extensible to incorporate additional components as the infrastructure evolves.<br/>- **Clarity and Maintainability:**  <br/>  All components and their interactions must be clearly labeled. The diagram code should be organized and modular to facilitate updates.<br/>- **Tool Compatibility:**  <br/>  The diagram must be generated using the Diagrams library in Python. All AWS services must use the latest icons provided by the library.<br/><br/>## Diagram Layout<br/>- **Account Clusters:**  <br/>  Separate clusters for each AWS account (Management, Development, Staging, Production) containing their respective resources.<br/>- **Networking &amp; Compute Components:**  <br/>  Within each account, group resources into a VPC cluster (with public and private subnets). Include connectivity arrows to show traffic flows (e.g., ALB \u2192 EKS, EKS \u2192 RDS).<br/>- **Static Frontend Hosting Setup:**  <br/>  Create a separate cluster to depict the CloudFront + S3 architecture for the React frontend. Connect this to the overall diagram to show it as part of the production ecosystem.<br/>- **Annotations:**  <br/>  Use clear labels to highlight CI/CD, remote access, and governance aspects.</span></pre><h1 id=\"eba8\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Step 2: The heavy lifting \u2014 Iterative development with Cursor</h1><p id=\"da9e\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">This is where Cursor\u2019s AI capabilities shine. Instead of manually writing all the code for the AWS resources, we can use Cursor to help us generate the code based on our requirements.</p><p id=\"bb3c\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">We will use in the Cursor agent the previously generated and modified RD/outline as a notepad in Cursor together with the architecture design document and Docs pointing to <a class=\"af hb\" href=\"https://diagrams.mingrammer.com/\" rel=\"noopener ugc nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Diagrams</a> docs pages.</p><figure class=\"qy qz ra rb rc oj ob oc paragraph-image\"><div role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"ok ol fj om bh on\"><div class=\"ob oc rl\"><picture><source srcSet=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:640/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 640w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:720/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 720w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:750/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 750w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:786/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 786w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:828/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 828w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1100/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 1100w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 1400w\" sizes=\"(min-resolution: 4dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 50vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 4) and (max-width: 700px) 50vw, (min-resolution: 3dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 67vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 3) and (max-width: 700px) 65vw, (min-resolution: 2.5dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 80vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2.5) and (max-width: 700px) 80vw, (min-resolution: 2dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 100vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2) and (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" type=\"image/webp\"/><source data-testid=\"og\" srcSet=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:640/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 640w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:720/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 720w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:750/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 750w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:786/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 786w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:828/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 828w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1100/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 1100w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/1*7yAUNQi1fkJr7BZdRPE4mg.png 1400w\" sizes=\"(min-resolution: 4dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 50vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 4) and (max-width: 700px) 50vw, (min-resolution: 3dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 67vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 3) and (max-width: 700px) 65vw, (min-resolution: 2.5dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 80vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2.5) and (max-width: 700px) 80vw, (min-resolution: 2dppx) and (max-width: 700px) 100vw, (-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2) and (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\"/><img alt=\"\" class=\"bh fu oo c\" width=\"700\" height=\"79\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"presentation\"/></picture></div></div></figure><p id=\"185f\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">Example prompt:</p><blockquote class=\"rm rn ro\"><p id=\"2dbc\" class=\"op oq rp or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">Based on the Requirements Document notes and Architecture Design notes, please write the code for generating diagrams. Make sure to follow the guidelines and examples from the diagrams documentation.</p></blockquote><h1 id=\"2a38\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Step 3: Initial implementation</h1><p id=\"a1e0\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Cursor started by importing the necessary components and setting up the basic structure:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"e61f\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\">from diagrams import Diagram, Cluster, Edge, Node<br/>from diagrams.aws.security import IAM, IdentityAndAccessManagementIam, Shield, Guardduty, WAF, SecretsManager<br/>from diagrams.aws.management import Organizations, Cloudtrail, Cloudwatch, SystemsManager, TrustedAdvisor, Config<br/>from diagrams.aws.network import ALB, NATGateway, ClientVpn, CloudFront, VPC, InternetGateway, Endpoint<br/>from diagrams.aws.compute import EKS, ECR<br/>from diagrams.aws.database import RDS<br/>from diagrams.aws.storage import S3<br/>from diagrams.aws.integration import Eventbridge, SQS<br/>from diagrams.aws.devtools import Codebuild<br/>from diagrams.onprem.ci import GithubActions<br/>from diagrams.onprem.gitops import ArgoCD<br/>from diagrams.onprem.vcs import Github<br/>from diagrams.onprem.monitoring import Datadog, Splunk<br/>from diagrams.aws.general import Users<br/>from diagrams.onprem.client import Users as DevOpsUsers<br/><br/># Define some custom colors for better visualization<br/>COLOR_MANAGEMENT = &quot;#009688&quot;  # Teal<br/>COLOR_DEV = &quot;#03A9F4&quot;         # Light Blue<br/>COLOR_STAGING = &quot;#FFC107&quot;     # Amber<br/>COLOR_PROD = &quot;#F44336&quot;        # Red<br/>COLOR_NETWORK = &quot;#8BC34A&quot;     # Light Green<br/>COLOR_COMPUTE = &quot;#673AB7&quot;     # Deep Purple<br/>COLOR_DATABASE = &quot;#FF9800&quot;    # Orange<br/>COLOR_FRONTEND = &quot;#9C27B0&quot;    # Purple<br/>COLOR_CICD = &quot;#795548&quot;        # Brown<br/>COLOR_MONITORING = &quot;#607D8B&quot;  # Blue Grey<br/>COLOR_SECURITY = &quot;#FF5722&quot;    # Deep Orange<br/>COLOR_USER = &quot;#000000&quot;        # Black<br/><br/>with Diagram(&quot;Innovate Inc. Cloud Architecture&quot;, show=False, direction=&quot;TB&quot;, outformat=[&quot;png&quot;]):<br/>    # External Users<br/>    end_users = Users(&quot;End Users&quot;)<br/>    developers = Users(&quot;Developers&quot;)<br/>    # GitHub (External)<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;GitHub (External)&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_CICD + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>        github = Github(&quot;Source Code&quot;)<br/>        ci_cd = GithubActions(&quot;CI/CD Pipelines&quot;)<br/>        github &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD) &gt;&gt; ci_cd<br/>        developers &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;Push Code&quot;) &gt;&gt; github<br/>    # Management Account<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Management Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MANAGEMENT + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        # Add management account resources here<br/>    # Development Account<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Development Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_DEV + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        # Add development account resources here<br/>    # Staging Account<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Staging Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_STAGING + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        # Add staging account resources here<br/>    # Production Account<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Production Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_PROD + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        # Add production account resources here</span></pre><h1 id=\"aa9f\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 1: Adding management account resources</h1><p id=\"f173\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Continued by adding resources to the Management Account:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"47ee\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Management Account (Master Account)<br/>with Cluster(&quot;Management Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MANAGEMENT + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>    orgs = Organizations(&quot;AWS Organizations&quot;)<br/>with Cluster(&quot;Centralized Management&quot;):<br/>        iam_identity = IdentityAndAccessManagementIam(&quot;IAM Identity Center&quot;)<br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Security Services&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_SECURITY + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>            guard_duty = Guardduty(&quot;GuardDuty&quot;)<br/>            trails = Cloudtrail(&quot;CloudTrail&quot;)<br/>            security_hub = Shield(&quot;Security Hub&quot;)<br/>            aws_config = Config(&quot;AWS Config&quot;)<br/>            trusted_advisor = TrustedAdvisor(&quot;Trusted Advisor&quot;)<br/>            secrets = SecretsManager(&quot;Secrets Manager&quot;)<br/>            # Connect security services<br/>            guard_duty - trails - security_hub<br/>            aws_config - trusted_advisor<br/>            secrets - security_hub<br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Monitoring &amp; Logs&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MONITORING + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>            logs = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch Logs&quot;)<br/>            metrics = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch Metrics&quot;)<br/>            ssm = SystemsManager(&quot;Systems Manager&quot;)<br/>            # Connect logging services<br/>            logs - metrics - ssm</span></pre><h1 id=\"2570\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 2: Adding account resources</h1><p id=\"5235\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Next, we added resources to each account. Here\u2019s an example for the Production Account:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"7aad\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Production Account<br/>with Cluster(&quot;Production Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_PROD + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>    prod_ecr = ECR(&quot;ECR Registry&quot;)<br/>    prod_vpn = ClientVpn(&quot;Production VPN&quot;)<br/>    prod_cwlogs = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch\\nLogs &amp; Metrics&quot;)<br/>with Cluster(&quot;VPC&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_NETWORK + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>        prod_igw = InternetGateway(&quot;Internet Gateway&quot;)<br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Public Subnets&quot;):<br/>            prod_alb = ALB(&quot;Load Balancer&quot;)<br/>            prod_nat = NATGateway(&quot;NAT Gateway&quot;)<br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Private Subnets&quot;):<br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Compute&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_COMPUTE + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                prod_eks = EKS(&quot;EKS Cluster&quot;)<br/>                with Cluster(&quot;In-Cluster Services&quot;):<br/>                    prod_argo = ArgoCD(&quot;ArgoCD&quot;)<br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Data&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_DATABASE + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                prod_rds = RDS(&quot;PostgreSQL&quot;)</span></pre><h1 id=\"8a40\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 3: Fixing import issues</h1><p id=\"a303\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">When I first ran the code, I encountered an import error with ArgoCD. Cursor helped me identify and fix the issue:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"79db\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Original incorrect import<br/>from diagrams.onprem.ci import ArgoCD<br/><br/># Fixed import<br/>from diagrams.onprem.gitops import ArgoCD</span></pre><h1 id=\"618f\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 4: Adding connections between components</h1><p id=\"ed51\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">I continued by adding connections between components to show data flow:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"e7d4\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Connect GitHub Actions to AWS Resources<br/>ci_cd &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD, label=&quot;Build &amp;\\nPush Images&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_ecr<br/><br/># Connect GitHub to ArgoCD instances<br/>github &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD) &gt;&gt; prod_argo<br/><br/># Connect ECR to EKS<br/>prod_ecr &gt;&gt; Edge(label=&quot;Pull\\nImages&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/><br/># Connect ALB to EKS<br/>prod_alb &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/>prod_eks &gt;&gt; prod_rds</span></pre><h1 id=\"a598\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 5: Enhancing the diagram</h1><p id=\"26f9\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Based on some feedback prompting, I made several enhancements:</p><ol class=\"\"><li id=\"aba2\" class=\"op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Added VPC endpoints for ECR access</li><li id=\"ae06\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Added CloudFront and S3 for static frontend hosting</li><li id=\"5d40\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Added user access paths</li><li id=\"7284\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Improved organization of clusters</li></ol><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"a0c7\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Static Frontend Hosting in Production<br/>with Cluster(&quot;Static Frontend Hosting&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_FRONTEND + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>    prod_frontend_s3 = S3(&quot;S3 Bucket\\n(React SPA)&quot;)<br/>    prod_frontend_cf = CloudFront(&quot;CloudFront CDN&quot;)<br/>    prod_frontend_cf &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_FRONTEND) &gt;&gt; prod_frontend_s3<br/>    end_users &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;Web\\nAccess&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_frontend_cf<br/><br/># VPC Endpoints for ECR access<br/>with Cluster(&quot;VPC Endpoints&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_NETWORK + &quot;30&quot;}):<br/>    prod_ecr_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;ECR API&quot;)<br/>    prod_ecr_dkr_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;ECR DKR&quot;)<br/>    prod_s3_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;S3&quot;)</span></pre><h1 id=\"2e2c\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Iteration 6: Simplifying the diagram</h1><p id=\"bd47\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">To improve clarity, I made several simplifications:</p><ol class=\"\"><li id=\"9e68\" class=\"op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Commented out Development and Staging environments to focus on Production</li><li id=\"debd\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Added an Account node to better represent the AWS account structure</li><li id=\"d4c6\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\">Fixed connections between AWS Organizations and account resources</li></ol><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"ddea\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># Management Account Connections to Account Clusters<br/>orgs &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Manage&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_account<br/><br/># IAM Identity Center Connections<br/>admin &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;SSO Login&quot;) &gt;&gt; iam_identity<br/>iam_identity &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Identity\\nFederation&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_account</span></pre><h1 id=\"9509\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Step 7: Handling connection challenges</h1><p id=\"97ac\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">One challenge I faced was connecting to Cluster objects directly, which isn\u2019t supported by the Diagrams library. I had to connect to nodes within clusters instead:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"0370\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\"># This doesn&#x27;t work:<br/>orgs &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Manage&quot;) &gt;&gt; Cluster(&quot;Production Account&quot;)<br/><br/># This works:<br/>orgs &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Manage&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_account</span></pre><h1 id=\"dd4d\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Step 8: Generating the diagram</h1><p id=\"f27c\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">To generate the diagram, run:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"2005\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\">python innovate_arch.py</span></pre><p id=\"9b84\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os ot ou ov ow ox oy oz gm pa pb pc gp pd pe pf gs pg ph pi pj ho bk\">This will create a PNG file in your project directory.</p><h1 id=\"273e\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Final code</h1><p id=\"b1dd\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Here\u2019s the complete code for our architecture diagram:</p><pre class=\"qy qz ra rb rc rd qw re bp rf bb bk\"><span id=\"83f5\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\">from diagrams import Diagram, Cluster, Edge, Node<br/>from diagrams.aws.security import IAM, IdentityAndAccessManagementIam, Shield, Guardduty, WAF, SecretsManager<br/>from diagrams.aws.management import Organizations, Cloudtrail, Cloudwatch, SystemsManager, TrustedAdvisor, Config<br/>from diagrams.aws.network import ALB, NATGateway, ClientVpn, CloudFront, VPC, InternetGateway, Endpoint<br/>from diagrams.aws.compute import EKS, ECR<br/>from diagrams.aws.database import RDS<br/>from diagrams.aws.storage import S3<br/>from diagrams.aws.integration import Eventbridge, SQS<br/>from diagrams.aws.devtools import Codebuild<br/>from diagrams.onprem.ci import GithubActions<br/>from diagrams.onprem.gitops import ArgoCD<br/>from diagrams.onprem.vcs import Github<br/>from diagrams.onprem.monitoring import Datadog, Splunk<br/>from diagrams.aws.general import Users<br/>from diagrams.onprem.client import Users as DevOpsUsers<br/><br/># Define some custom colors for better visualization<br/>COLOR_MANAGEMENT = &quot;#009688&quot;  # Teal<br/>COLOR_DEV = &quot;#03A9F4&quot;         # Light Blue<br/>COLOR_STAGING = &quot;#FFC107&quot;     # Amber<br/>COLOR_PROD = &quot;#F44336&quot;        # Red<br/>COLOR_NETWORK = &quot;#8BC34A&quot;     # Light Green<br/>COLOR_COMPUTE = &quot;#673AB7&quot;     # Deep Purple<br/>COLOR_DATABASE = &quot;#FF9800&quot;    # Orange<br/>COLOR_FRONTEND = &quot;#9C27B0&quot;    # Purple<br/>COLOR_CICD = &quot;#795548&quot;        # Brown<br/>COLOR_MONITORING = &quot;#607D8B&quot;  # Blue Grey<br/>COLOR_SECURITY = &quot;#FF5722&quot;    # Deep Orange<br/>COLOR_USER = &quot;#000000&quot;        # Black<br/><br/>with Diagram(&quot;Innovate Inc. Cloud Architecture&quot;, show=False, direction=&quot;TB&quot;, outformat=[&quot;png&quot;]):<br/>    # External Users<br/>    end_users = Users(&quot;End Users&quot;)<br/>    admin = Users(&quot;Admin&quot;)<br/>    <br/>    # GitHub (External)<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;GitHub (External)&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_CICD + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>        github = Github(&quot;Source Code&quot;)<br/>        ci_cd = GithubActions(&quot;CI/CD Pipelines&quot;)<br/>        <br/>        github &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD) &gt;&gt; ci_cd<br/>        admin &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;Push Code&quot;) &gt;&gt; github<br/>    <br/>    # Management Account (Master Account)<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Management Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MANAGEMENT + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        orgs = Organizations(&quot;AWS Organizations&quot;)<br/>        <br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Centralized Management&quot;):<br/>            iam_identity = IdentityAndAccessManagementIam(&quot;IAM Identity Center&quot;)<br/>            <br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Security Services&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_SECURITY + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                guard_duty = Guardduty(&quot;GuardDuty&quot;)<br/>                trails = Cloudtrail(&quot;CloudTrail&quot;)<br/>                security_hub = Shield(&quot;Security Hub&quot;)<br/>                aws_config = Config(&quot;AWS Config&quot;)<br/>                trusted_advisor = TrustedAdvisor(&quot;Trusted Advisor&quot;)<br/>                secrets = SecretsManager(&quot;Secrets Manager&quot;)<br/>                <br/>                # Connect security services<br/>                guard_duty - trails - security_hub<br/>                aws_config - trusted_advisor<br/>                secrets - security_hub<br/><br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Monitoring &amp; Logs&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MONITORING + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                logs = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch Logs&quot;)<br/>                metrics = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch Metrics&quot;)<br/>                ssm = SystemsManager(&quot;Systems Manager&quot;)<br/>                <br/>                # Connect logging services<br/>                logs - metrics - ssm<br/>    <br/>    # Third-party Monitoring (External to AWS)<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Third-Party Monitoring&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_MONITORING + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        datadog = Datadog(&quot;Datadog\\nMonitoring&quot;)<br/>        splunk = Splunk(&quot;Splunk\\nLog Analytics&quot;)<br/>        <br/>        # Connect monitoring<br/>        datadog - splunk<br/>    <br/>    # Production Account<br/>    with Cluster(&quot;Production Account&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_PROD + &quot;10&quot;}):<br/>        prod_account = Node(&quot;Account&quot;)<br/>        prod_\r\n5121\r\necr = ECR(&quot;ECR Registry&quot;)<br/>        prod_vpn = ClientVpn(&quot;Production VPN&quot;)<br/>        prod_cwlogs = Cloudwatch(&quot;CloudWatch\\nLogs &amp; Metrics&quot;)<br/>        prod_secrets = SecretsManager(&quot;Secrets Manager&quot;)<br/>        <br/>        # Static Frontend Hosting in Production<br/>        with Cluster(&quot;Static Frontend Hosting&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_FRONTEND + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>            prod_frontend_s3 = S3(&quot;S3 Bucket\\n(React SPA)&quot;)<br/>            prod_frontend_cf = CloudFront(&quot;CloudFront CDN&quot;)<br/>            prod_frontend_cf &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_FRONTEND) &gt;&gt; prod_frontend_s3<br/>            end_users &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;Web\\nAccess&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_frontend_cf<br/>        <br/>        with Cluster(&quot;VPC&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_NETWORK + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>            prod_igw = InternetGateway(&quot;Internet Gateway&quot;)<br/>            <br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Public Subnets&quot;):<br/>                prod_alb = ALB(&quot;Load Balancer&quot;)<br/>                prod_nat = NATGateway(&quot;NAT Gateway&quot;)<br/>            <br/>            with Cluster(&quot;Private Subnets&quot;):<br/>                with Cluster(&quot;VPC Endpoints&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_NETWORK + &quot;30&quot;}):<br/>                    prod_ecr_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;ECR API&quot;)<br/>                    prod_ecr_dkr_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;ECR DKR&quot;)<br/>                    prod_s3_endpoint = Endpoint(&quot;S3&quot;)<br/>                <br/>                with Cluster(&quot;Compute&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_COMPUTE + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                    prod_eks = EKS(&quot;EKS Cluster&quot;)<br/>                    <br/>                    with Cluster(&quot;In-Cluster Services&quot;):<br/>                        prod_argo = ArgoCD(&quot;ArgoCD&quot;)<br/>                        prod_eso = Node(&quot;External\\nSecrets\\nOperator&quot;)<br/>                        prod_argo - prod_eso<br/>                        prod_eso &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_SECURITY, style=&quot;dashed&quot;, label=&quot;Pull Secrets&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_secrets<br/>                <br/>                with Cluster(&quot;Data&quot;, graph_attr={&quot;bgcolor&quot;: COLOR_DATABASE + &quot;20&quot;}):<br/>                    prod_rds = RDS(&quot;PostgreSQL&quot;)<br/>    <br/>    # Event Bus for Log Integration<br/>    event_bridge = Eventbridge(&quot;EventBridge&quot;)<br/>    log_queue = SQS(&quot;Log Queue&quot;)<br/>    <br/>    # Connect GitHub Actions to AWS Resources - Building and Pushing Images<br/>    ci_cd &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD, label=&quot;Build &amp;\\nPush Images&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_ecr<br/>    <br/>    # Connect GitHub to ArgoCD instances<br/>    github &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_CICD) &gt;&gt; prod_argo<br/>    <br/>    # Connect ECR to EKS via VPC Endpoints<br/>    prod_ecr &gt;&gt; Edge(label=&quot;Pull\\nImages&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_ecr_endpoint &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/>    <br/>    # Management Account Connections to Account Clusters<br/>    orgs &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Manage&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_account<br/>    <br/>    # Production Account Connections - ALB only<br/>    end_users &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;API Access&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_alb<br/>    prod_alb &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/>    prod_eks &gt;&gt; prod_rds<br/>    <br/>    # Connect CloudWatch to Resources<br/>    prod_eks &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MONITORING, label=&quot;Logs &amp;\\nMetrics&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_cwlogs<br/>    <br/>    # Connect CloudWatch to Central Logging<br/>    prod_cwlogs &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MONITORING, label=&quot;Centralized\\nLogging&quot;) &gt;&gt; logs<br/>    <br/>    # Connect EKS Pods to Splunk<br/>    prod_eks &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MONITORING, style=&quot;dashed&quot;, label=&quot;Pod\\nLogs&quot;) &gt;&gt; event_bridge &gt;&gt; log_queue &gt;&gt; splunk<br/>    <br/>    # Connect Resources to Datadog Monitoring<br/>    datadog &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MONITORING, style=&quot;dashed&quot;, label=&quot;Monitor\\nMetrics&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/>    datadog &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MONITORING, style=&quot;dashed&quot;, label=&quot;Monitor\\nMetrics&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_rds<br/>    <br/>    # Connect Security Services to Resources<br/>    guard_duty &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_SECURITY, style=&quot;dotted&quot;, label=&quot;Security\\nMonitoring&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/><br/>    # Admin VPN Access<br/>    admin &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;VPN\\nAccess&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_vpn<br/>    prod_vpn &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER) &gt;&gt; prod_eks<br/><br/>    # IAM Identity Center Connections<br/>    admin &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_USER, label=&quot;SSO Login&quot;) &gt;&gt; iam_identity<br/>    iam_identity &gt;&gt; Edge(color=COLOR_MANAGEMENT, label=&quot;Identity\\nFederation&quot;) &gt;&gt; prod_account</span></pre><h1 id=\"472a\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Tips for using Cursor with Diagrams library</h1><ol class=\"\"><li id=\"4d78\" class=\"op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Use Notepads for requirements</strong>: Create a notepad in Cursor to document your requirements and architecture decisions.</li><li id=\"6c25\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Leverage AI for code generation</strong>: Ask Cursor to help you generate code for specific parts of your diagram.</li><li id=\"be55\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Iterative development</strong>: Start with a basic structure and iteratively add more details.</li><li id=\"c69d\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Fix errors incrementally</strong>: When you encounter errors, fix them one at a time and run the code after each fix.</li><li id=\"323d\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Use color coding</strong>: Define custom colors to make your diagram more readable and visually appealing.</li><li id=\"69c2\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Organize with Clusters</strong>: Use nested clusters to group related resources.</li><li id=\"afe5\" class=\"op oq is or b os qo ou ov ow qp oy oz gm qq pb pc gp qr pe pf gs qs ph pi pj qx qm qn bk\"><strong class=\"or it\">Add meaningful labels</strong>: Use edge labels to explain the purpose of connections.</li></ol><h1 id=\"a33b\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Bonus diagram</h1><p id=\"7a42\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Playing around with different Diagram as Code libraries and tools, I figured Cursor and ChatGPT are quite good at generating <a class=\"af hb\" href=\"https://www.mermaidchart.com/\" rel=\"noopener ugc nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Mermaid Charts</a> too!</p><figure class=\"qy qz ra rb rc oj ob oc paragraph-image\"><div role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" class=\"ok ol fj om bh on\"><div class=\"ob oc rq\"><picture><source srcSet=\"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:640/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 640w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:720/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 720w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:750/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 750w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:786/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 786w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:828/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 828w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1100/format:webp/1*5DdhV-kDgdQ9w6LJStzA8w.png 1100w, https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize