pan id=\"fb1c\" class=\"rg pl is qw b bg rh ri l rj rk\">---<br/>config:<br/>  layout: dagre<br/>  theme: default<br/>---<br/>flowchart TD<br/> subgraph subGraph0[&quot;Security Account&quot;]<br/>        C1[&quot;CloudTrail - Central Logs&quot;]<br/>        C2[&quot;GuardDuty&quot;]<br/>        C3[&quot;AWS Config&quot;]<br/>        C4[&quot;Security Hub&quot;]<br/>  end<br/> subgraph subGraph1[&quot;Production Account&quot;]<br/>        D1[&quot;VPC - Private Subnets&quot;]<br/>        D2[&quot;Multi-AZ RDS Cluster&quot;]<br/>        D3[&quot;RDS Proxy&quot;]<br/>        D4[&quot;BI RDS Instance&quot;]<br/>        D5[&quot;VPN&quot;]<br/>  end<br/> subgraph subGraph2[&quot;On-Premises Environment&quot;]<br/>        O1[&quot;On-Prem Application Servers&quot;]<br/>  end<br/>    A[&quot;AWS Organization&quot;] --&gt; B(&quot;Management Account&quot;) &amp; C(&quot;Security Account&quot;) &amp; D(&quot;Production Account&quot;) &amp; E(&quot;Dev/Test Account&quot;) &amp; F(&quot;Shared Services/Networking Account&quot;) &amp; S[&quot;AWS SSO / IAM&quot;]<br/>    O1 -- IPsec VPN --&gt; D5<br/>    D5 --&gt; D1<br/>    D1 --&gt; D2 &amp; D3 &amp; D4<br/>    D2 -- replication --&gt; D4<br/>    D3 --&gt; D2<br/>    D2 -- API &amp; DB Logs --&gt; C1<br/>    D2 -- Threat Data --&gt; C2<br/>    D2 -- Config Data --&gt; C3<br/>    S --&gt; B &amp; C &amp; D &amp; E &amp; F</span></pre><h1 id=\"6bd2\" class=\"pk pl is bf pm pn po pp gj pq pr ps gl pt pu pv pw px py pz qa qb qc qd qe qf bk\">Conclusion</h1><p id=\"1721\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragraph op oq is or b os qg ou ov ow qh oy oz gm qi pb pc gp qj pe pf gs qk ph pi pj ho bk\">Using Python\u2019s Diagrams library or Mermaid Charts with Cursor provides a powerful way to create and maintain cloud architecture diagrams or quick flow charts. The code-based approach ensures that your diagrams can evolve alongside your infrastructure, making it an excellent choice for DevOps teams.</p><p id=\"5ead\" class=\"pw-post-body-paragr